 "observations": [
  "The page number «130» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the left the number of the table, «Tab. 19», in bold sans serif, underlined. The three titles (L01-L03), in bold, the sigla in roman: L01 that of O, L02 that of C, L03 that of N; «gavzehar», «iavzehar», the Persian-Arabic word for the node (Suter, p. 41, JP2 0073). The folios of the manuscripts, «C 52r-v, O 109v,» over «N 23v.», stand at the left of L02 and L03, the letters raised; here as left margin notes beside L01-L03, divided so that they keep within the page. The page has no signature.",
  "The table: a thick and a thin rule above the head, a double rule below it; vertical rules divide the fifteen columns, double ones before and after the columns of the years and of the months; thin rules under the heads that span the four columns of signs, degrees, minutes and seconds, whose heads «Sig.», «Gr.», «Min.», «Sec.» are set in small bold type, only the first «Min.» and «Sec.» with note numbers. «Anni collecti» and «Anni plani» are printed turned through a quarter, reading upwards, in two lines, «Menses arabum» in two lines; here their words stand in L04 and L05. Each printed row is one line here, the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The collected years end with 570 (L26), the months with Dulheia (L18). «Jumedi I.» and «Jumedi II.» both carry the note number 7, whose lemma «Jumedi» covers both.",
  "L07-L36. The node moves backwards; the table gives its motion as a growing quantity, which is subtracted from 360° to give the place of the node, as Suter computes on p. 59 (JP2 0091, «360° — 279° 41′ … da der Drachenkopf retrograd ist»), with the values 92° 39′ for the end of the year 510 and 184° 42′ for 29 years, those of L24 and L35. Brahmagupta's parameter, 232 311 168 revolutions of the node in 1 577 916 450 000 days, gives 3′ 10″ 48‴ 20⁗ a day and 6s 23° 27′ 34.2″ in 30 Arab years (10 631 days). Checked: the table rests on a slightly larger motion, 3′ 10″ 48‴ 23⁗ a day, 6s 23° 27′ 42.6″ in 30 years (the single year 30, 6s 23° 27′ 43″): with it the collected years from the radix 7s 23° 47′ 38″ agree to within 1.5″ (with the readings of notes a-d), the single years, 354 days and 355 in the leap years 2, 5, 7, 10, 13, 16, 18, 21, 24, 26 and 29, to within 1.5″ (with the readings of notes e-g), and the months to within 1.1″ (with the readings of notes h, i, k and l; the edition's 15 of note k, N's reading against the 35 of C and O, is required, 6° 15′ 15″). Against Brahmagupta's parameter the collected years run ahead by about 8.8″ in each row, 2′ 39″ at 570.",
  "L24, the single year 18, 11s 8° 5′ 13″: the seconds are 40 too small; the year 17, 10s 19° 16′ 58″, and a leap year of 355 days, 18° 48′ 55″, give 11s 8° 5′ 53″ (computed with the table's motion 11s 8° 5′ 53.9″), and the year 19, 11s 26° 51′ 39″, follows from 53″, not from 13″. No note bears on them.",
  "N06: after «h) 22] C,» a small raised mark like an apostrophe (4 × 9 px) stands before «13 O»; not transcribed. N04: a speck after «Dulkada]»; not transcribed. N03: «Răth», with a breve over the a; «Gum’», «Scaw’», «Dulk’», «Dulh’», with the apostrophe. Italics: «V. notas in tab. 8.»."
 ],
